Inheritance polymorphism
Inheritance polymorphism allows for functionality to be determined at runtime in a similar
way to an interface but applies to class inheritance. In our example, a pet can be fed, so we
can define this as having a new Feed(IPetFood) method, which uses the interface that
was defined previously:
public virtual void Feed(IPetFood food)
{
Eat(food);
}
protected void Eat(IPetFood food)
{
_hunger -= food.Energy;
}
